explanation:
This definition does not formalize a notion from the literature. It is plumbing for the library's construction of the third Reidemeister move on PD-codes. It composes three maps:
- the embedding `c × id` on `Fin 3 × Fin 4`;
- the crossing/slot equivalence `crossingSlotEquiv n`;
- the PD-code's half-edge labelling `D.halfEdge`.

The result maps each (selected crossing, slot) pair to its half-edge, so `triangleEmbedding D c (i, s) = D.crossing (c i) s`, as the next lemma `triangleEmbedding_apply` states. Its only job is to lift the local twelve-slot permutation `reidemeisterThreeSlots` to a permutation of all half-edges, via `Perm.viaFintypeEmbedding`. It is an implementation detail of the construction, not a mathematical object.
